to reasonable levels or stops them entirely sometimes. The overall effect of policies aimed at decommodifying housing, of course, is to make it harder to profit off of housing. You would curb speculation and reduce or eliminate profits possible from rent seeking. Effectively, the goal is to make housing useless as an investment and therefore useful only to put people in.

